### 6.2 Track Selection

Because J/\(\Psi\) is a heavy particle, with a short lifetime of \(\tau=7.2\times 10^{-21}\) s and a decay length of \(c\tau=2.2\times 10^{-12}\) m, which is much smaller than the TPC tracking resolution at the vertex, J/\(\Psi\)s are assumed to decay at the vertex position. Therefore, only tracks that project back to the primary vertex, known as primary tracks, were used in this analysis. This section presents cuts that remove poorly reconstructed tracks that are not reconstructed in the primary vertex.

