### 6.4 Efficiency and Acceptance Corrections

Due to the finite precision and acceptance of the STAR detector, not all the J/\(\Psi\)s created in a collision were correctly reconstructed. The loss of J/\(\Psi\)s is caused by several different sources:

(1) _Acceptance losses._ The TPC is not able to reconstruct a J/\(\Psi\) if, for example, one of the daughter electrons has a pseudorapidity \(|\eta|>1\). The fraction of the total

